---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const desc = 'Free data center build cost calculator: capital cost per megawatt for electrical, mechanical and shell, plus land and contingency, and cost per rack at your density.';
const jsonld = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebApplication',
  name: 'Data Center Build Cost Calculator', applicationCategory: 'BusinessApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Web', offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
  url: 'https://theworldofai.org/calculators/datacenter-capex/',
});
---
<Base title="Data Center Build Cost Calculator: cost per megawatt — The World of AI" description={desc} current="/calculators/" jsonld={jsonld}>
  <h1>Data Center Build Cost Calculator</h1>
  <p class="answer">Data center construction is priced per megawatt of IT capacity, not per square foot, because the electrical and mechanical plant dominates the cost. Published ranges cluster around $7 to $12 million per MW for a conventional build and higher for dense liquid-cooled AI halls, with the shell itself a minority of the total.</p>
  <p class="meta-line">Formula and defaults last reviewed: 2026-08-31.</p>

  <div class="calc">
    <label>IT capacity (MW) <input type="number" id="mw" value="20" step="1" min="0.1" /></label>
    <label>Electrical and mechanical cost ($ per MW) <input type="number" id="permw" value="8500000" step="250000" min="0" /></label>
    <label>Building area (sq ft) <input type="number" id="sqft" value="180000" step="5000" min="0" /></label>
    <label>Shell and fit-out ($ per sq ft) <input type="number" id="shell" value="180" step="10" min="0" /></label>
    <label>Land and site works ($) <input type="number" id="land" value="12000000" step="500000" min="0" /></label>
    <label>Contingency (%) <input type="number" id="cont" value="10" step="1" min="0" /></label>
    <label>Rack density for the cost-per-rack view (kW) <input type="number" id="density" value="12" step="1" min="0.5" /></label>
    <div class="out" id="out" aria-live="polite"></div>
  </div>

  <h2>How the math works</h2>
  <p>Total = (MW × cost per MW) + (area × cost per sq ft) + land, plus contingency. The cost per
    MW line carries the switchgear, generators, UPS, distribution and the entire cooling plant,
    which is why it dominates: a data hall is an electrical and mechanical building with a roof
    on it, not an office with servers inside.</p>
  <h2>What moves the number most</h2>
  <p>Redundancy topology: 2N electrical roughly doubles the most expensive line. Cooling
    approach: liquid cooling adds CDUs and secondary loops but removes chiller and air-handling
    capacity, so the direction of the change depends on the design. Region: labour, permitting
    and seismic or wind requirements move totals by a wide margin between markets. And the
    grid connection, which is often the longest lead item and is sometimes not a capital cost
    to the developer at all but a queue position that cannot be bought.</p>
  <h2>What this does not tell you</h2>
  <p>These are construction costs and exclude IT equipment entirely. For an AI build the servers
    and accelerators usually cost several times the building that houses them, so a capital plan
    that stops at the shell is missing most of the money.</p>

  <h2>A worked example</h2>
  <p>A 20 MW hall at $8.5 million per MW for electrical and mechanical plant runs $170 million
    before the building itself. At 180,000 square feet and $180 per square foot for shell and
    fit-out, the structure adds another $32.4 million, and $12 million in land and site work
    brings the subtotal to $214.4 million. A 10 percent contingency, which is thin for a first
    build and common for a repeat design at a known site, adds $21.4 million for a total of
    roughly $236 million, or about $11.8 million per megawatt all-in. At 12 kW per rack that
    campus holds around 1,667 rack positions, putting capital cost per rack near $141,000
    before a single server is racked.</p>

  <h2>Where the per-megawatt figure comes from</h2>
  <p>Published estimates for hyperscale and colocation construction have clustered in the
    $7 to $12 million per MW range for several years, reported by data centre construction
    and real estate advisory firms tracking completed projects across North America. The range
    reflects redundancy level, region and the split between electrical and mechanical scope
    that a developer buys as turnkey versus self-performs. AI-dense halls built for liquid
    cooling and higher rack power have generally landed above that range, since the cooling
    plant and power delivery both scale with density rather than floor area, and this
    calculator's default is set toward the middle of the conventional band rather than the
    AI-dense one, adjustable by moving the cost-per-MW figure up for a liquid-cooled design.</p>

  <div class="cite-box">Cite this tool: <code>"Data Center Build Cost Calculator." The World of AI,
    theworldofai.org/calculators/datacenter-capex/.</code></div>

  <script is:inline>
  (function () {
    function n(i) { return parseFloat(document.getElementById(i).value) || 0; }
    function f(v, d) { return v.toLocaleString(undefined, { maximumFractionDigits: d === undefined ? 0 : d }); }
    var IDS = ['mw','permw','sqft','shell','land','cont','density'];
    function calc() {
      var mep = n('mw') * n('permw');
      var shell = n('sqft') * n('shell');
      var sub = mep + shell + n('land');
      var total = sub * (1 + n('cont') / 100);
      var perMw = n('mw') > 0 ? total / n('mw') : 0;
      var racks = n('density') > 0 ? (n('mw') * 1000) / n('density') : 0;
      document.getElementById('out').innerHTML =
        'Electrical and mechanical: <b>$' + f(mep) + '</b><br>' +
        'Shell and fit-out: $' + f(shell) + ' &nbsp;·&nbsp; land and site: $' + f(n('land')) + '<br>' +
        'Total with ' + f(n('cont')) + '% contingency: <b>$' + f(total) + '</b><br>' +
        'All-in cost per MW: <b>$' + f(perMw) + '</b><br>' +
        '<span class="sub">About ' + f(racks) + ' racks at ' + f(n('density')) + ' kW, roughly $' + f(racks > 0 ? total / racks : 0) + ' of capital per rack position.</span>';
    }
    IDS.forEach(function (i) {
      document.getElementById(i).addEventListener('input', calc);
      document.getElementById(i).addEventListener('change', calc);
    });
    calc();
  })();
  </script>
  <style>
    .calc { border: 1px solid #e6e4de; border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 20px; background: #fafaf6; margin: 1.4em 0; }
    .calc label { display: block; margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 14px; color: #26262b; }
    .calc input, .calc select { display: block; margin-top: 4px; padding: 7px 9px; font-size: 15px;
      border: 1px solid #cfcdc6; border-radius: 6px; width: 220px; max-width: 100%; }
    .out { margin-top: 14px; padding-top: 14px; border-top: 1px solid #e6e4de; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; }
    .out b { color: #201868; }
    .sub { color: #7A8A9E; font-size: 13.5px; }
  </style>
</Base>
